{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"mazie","id":"366565198284324868","is_bot":0,"username":"damnzam"},"author_id":"366565198284324868","channel_id":"647890633763323924","content":"The image is hazy, as if even Vee doesn't recall this scene perfectly. Her memory has been Modified too many times before, but there is always one constant when she starts to recall. \n\nYou see the interior of a shop in a small village just outside of London. There is ash everywhere, and a clearing right where two figures lie. Vee, a few years younger though you're not quite sure how many years exactly. Her hair is shorter ending just around her chin.\n\nVee lies on the floor, cradled in the arms of a man who looks quite similar to her, her brother and last of her family.\n\nThis is Vee's first ever memory. \n\n\"Vee? Vee, wake up.\"\n\nStirring, she does. She opens her mouth, tries to call out for anything, but struggles to remember as it catches in her throat. Remember? Remember anything. She can't even remember how to speak.\n\n\"Viorica.\" He tells her her name. It sounds beautiful. It sounds right. His eyes are blue like the summer sky, against the light of her own green. But his face is hers, and her face is his. Ghosts of her past linger in the back of her head, nameless and faceless and taunting in her dreams; but her past and the emptiness of it do not seem to matter to him.\n\nThe scenes continue in fast-forward, scrubbing away the man from every scene. Teaching her to walk, teaching her to speak. When the summer heat is at its worst, the pair escape to the woods, or swim in the nearby muddy creek, or they lie for hours in the meadow they call theirs, watching the sun pass from overhead. All of them memories from a face too much like her own... but a name she will no longer place.\n\nSeeing these memories again, for what is going to be the last time, for this split second, Vee feels infinite, she is everywhere. For this split second, she remembers it all.\n\nAnd then breaks into a million pieces, and only one comes back. Hollow and incomplete, but she is back. She is here and alive. And the split second is over, and she can't remember anymore.","created_at":"2020-07-30T03:56:51.011000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-30T05:26:41.920000Z","id":"738243687527481398","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
