{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"647890633763323924","content":"A scene flashes before you. Web is standing in a sewer basin, looking up at someone above them. Through the grate above them you can see a young mousy child doing a small performance with a set of balls. Web smiles, and the figure looks down. \n\"Hello?\" The figure asks.\nWeb pokes their head out of the grate and reaches a hand to shake. \"You're pretty young to be out here alone by yourself. What's your name?\"\n\"My name? Umm, I calls meself Skitter.\"\nMore memories flash by as you watch Web see Skitter grow from a scared street rat to a young man with friends he made himself.\nYou see Web bringing him food so he doesn't go hungry.\nWeb showing Skitter the sewers for the first time, his eyes wide in amazement at the massive farms down below.\nWeb making Skitter a jacket from spider silk and scavenged brown fabric.\nWeb meeting up with Skitter on the rooftops to talk about city life.\nMany late night talks spent up there.\nSkitter's tenth birthday, Web managing to get all the ingredients together to make a small cake.\nThe first time Web met Skitter's mouse friend.\nWeb repairing the jacket after a nasty run-in with the Redcoats. \nWeb finding Skitter beat up one night and nursing him back to health. \nSkitter giving Web a cake they 'acquired' for Web's 18th birthday.\nWeb meeting Skitter's new friends through him. \nWeb giving Skitter's mouse the top hat.\nSkitter telling Web they were a shifter too\nWeb boarding the Tir Na Nog, worried about Skitter making in on, board\nWeb starting work on Skitter's binder.\nWeb watching Skitter and Wren dance just hours before.\nInstead of those, Web remembers being alone. Growing up in the sewers with no friends on the surface. \nNever finding anyone like them.\nStill living without ever knowing what they really are.\nBeing scared of never finding someone who understands all they've been through. \nThe Web who knows Skitter grew up loved and accepted, understood for who they were.\nThe Web who has forgotten Skitter had none of those things.","created_at":"2020-07-30T04:03:55.759000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-30T05:08:57.770000Z","id":"738245469049716737","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
